From: Remora <noreply@localhost>
Date: Tue, 4 Aug 2026 22:05:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] gbm_mesa: tell the external allocator codec buffers must be linear

bd remora-cq3. On bare/NVIDIA the video path spans BOTH GPUs: c2-va decodes
and encodes on the Intel xe VF (iHD, renderD129) while SurfaceFlinger
composites on NVIDIA. The external (vtest) allocator runs on NVIDIA, so it
hands codec buffers back in NVIDIA's block-linear layout -- which iHD cannot
import:

  Output buffer info: drmFormat=XB24 modifier=0x300000000606014 fromHandle=1
  vaCreateSurfaces(DRM_PRIME_2, modifier=0x300000000606014) failed:
      resource allocation failed
  Failed to copy VA surface into output frame.
  DecodeComponent: reportError(error=14)

The decoder fails on its first output frame, the app sees
ERROR_CODE_DECODING_FAILED and restarts the player once per segment: audio
rebuilds every ~10s and the picture never moves.

The combination table already states this contract locally -- 0003 advertises
BO_USE_HW_VIDEO_DECODER on the 32bpp RGB formats with linear_metadata, and the
encoder combos above it do the same -- but linear_metadata only governs
minigbm's own bookkeeping. The external allocator never consults it, and the
wire carried only "mappable" and "scanout", neither of which means "another
device reads this". So the contract was declared and then dropped at the
boundary.

Carry it explicitly. force_linear already exists but means "the CPU maps it",
which is a different question with a different answer: the host ranks a
foreign import ABOVE scanout and a CPU map BELOW it, so the two cannot share a
flag. Decode is the RGBX output pool, encode the VDENC direct-RGB source.

Pairs with venus-nvidia patch 0023, which adds
VCMD_ALLOC_GPU_FLAG_LINEAR_REQUIRED and honours it. struct alloc_args is the
ABI between gralloc.minigbm_gbm_mesa.so and libgbm_mesa_wrapper.so, so both
must be rebuilt and shipped together.

---
diff --git a/gbm_mesa_driver/gbm_mesa_internals.cpp b/gbm_mesa_driver/gbm_mesa_internals.cpp
index 9381d76898cfcc27ed291fee9c0a15d2787a4b5e..4bbb900a03f5469d247f0dd0deaf00677156fae4 100644
--- a/gbm_mesa_driver/gbm_mesa_internals.cpp
+++ b/gbm_mesa_driver/gbm_mesa_internals.cpp
@@ -376,6 +376,27 @@ int gbm_mesa_bo_create(struct bo *bo, uint32_t width, uint32_t height, uint32_t
 		.force_linear = (use_flags & BO_USE_SW_MASK) != 0,
 		.needs_map_stride = (use_flags & BO_USE_SW_MASK) != 0,
 		.use_scanout = (use_flags & BO_USE_SCANOUT) != 0,
+		/*
+		 * The codec buffers cross a device boundary and the allocator has to
+		 * be told, because it cannot see it (bd remora-cq3).
+		 *
+		 * On bare/NVIDIA video is split across BOTH GPUs: c2-va decodes and
+		 * encodes on the Intel xe VF while SurfaceFlinger composites on
+		 * NVIDIA. The external (vtest) allocator runs on NVIDIA, so a codec
+		 * buffer it hands back in NVIDIA's block-linear layout is refused by
+		 * iHD on import -- "vaCreateSurfaces(DRM_PRIME_2, modifier=...)
+		 * failed: resource allocation failed" -- and the decoder reports
+		 * error 14 on its first output frame, which the app sees as
+		 * ERROR_CODE_DECODING_FAILED. Linear is the only layout both agree on.
+		 *
+		 * The combination table above already says exactly this locally, by
+		 * advertising the HW_VIDEO_* usages on the 32bpp RGB formats with
+		 * linear_metadata; this carries the same contract to an allocator
+		 * that does not consult it. Decode is the RGBX output pool, encode is
+		 * the VDENC direct-RGB source.
+		 */
+		.linear_required =
+		    (use_flags & (BO_USE_HW_VIDEO_DECODER | BO_USE_HW_VIDEO_ENCODER)) != 0,
 	};
 
 	/* Alignment for RPI4 CSI camera. Since we do not care about other cameras, keep this
diff --git a/gbm_mesa_driver/gbm_mesa_wrapper.h b/gbm_mesa_driver/gbm_mesa_wrapper.h
index 653cb8ea35d54d580688f6a679d596636cc686a5..932e442609fedafa5ec8464eb921d4a4e18e359c 100644
--- a/gbm_mesa_driver/gbm_mesa_wrapper.h
+++ b/gbm_mesa_driver/gbm_mesa_wrapper.h
@@ -29,6 +29,11 @@ struct alloc_args {
 	bool use_scanout;
 	bool force_linear;
 	bool needs_map_stride;
+	/* A second GPU imports this buffer, so linear is the only layout both
+	 * understand. Distinct from force_linear, which means "the CPU maps it":
+	 * the external allocator ranks this above scanout, and force_linear below
+	 * it (bd remora-cq3). */
+	bool linear_required;
 	int out_fd;
 	uint32_t out_stride;
 	uint64_t out_modifier;
